{"d":823,"id":"thoughts/cutedsl","store":"note","title":"CuTeDSL","date":"2025-12-12","prec":"day","total":2,"part":48,"chunks":[{"r":4426,"c":0,"text":"A Tensor is specified by an _iterator_ and a _layout_:\n\n$$\nL = S : D\n$$\n\nwhere $S$ denotes the _shape_ of the tensor, and $D$ denotes the _strides_ of the tensor\n\nFor example:\n\nrow-major versus col-major","m":1},{"r":4427,"c":1,"text":"$$\n\\begin{array}{ccc}\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\n\\hline\n0 & 1 & 2 & 3 & 4 & 5 \\\\\n\\hline\n6 & 7 & 8 & 9 & 10 & 11 \\\\\n\\hline\n12 & 13 & 14 & 15 & 16 & 17 \\\\\n\\hline\n18 & 19 & 20 & 21 & 22 & 23 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n&\n\\hspace{3em}\n&\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\n\\hline\n0 & 4 & 8 & 12 & 16 & 20 \\\\\n\\hline\n1 & 5 & 9 & 13 & 17 & 21 \\\\\n\\hline\n2 & 6 & 10 & 14 & 18 & 22 \\\\\n\\hline\n3 & 7 & 11 & 15 & 19 & 23 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\\\[1em]\nL = (4,6) : (6,1) & & L = (4,6) : (1,4)\n\\end{array}\n$$\n\nbroadcast versus strides\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{ccc}\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\n\\hline\n0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\\n\\hline\n1 & 1 & 1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\\n\\hline\n2 & 2 & 2 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\\n\\hline\n3 & 3 & 3 & 3 & 3 & 3 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n&\n\\hspace{3em}\n&\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\n\\hline\n0 & 1 & 2 & 3 & 4 & 5 \\\\\n\\hline\n12 & 13 & 14 & 15 & 16 & 17 \\\\\n\\hline\n24 & 25 & 26 & 27 & 28 & 29 \\\\\n\\hline\n36 & 37 & 38 & 39 & 40 & 41 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\\\[1em]\nL = (4,6) : (1,0) & & L = (4,6) : (12,1)\n\\end{array}\n$$","m":1}]}